# AgentMaster dependency pins (optional supply-chain guard)
#
# By default the auto-updater pulls the latest default branch of every
# third-party skill repo every 6 hours — which means a compromised upstream
# repo would flow straight into your ~/.claude/skills/. Pinning a repo locks
# it to an exact, reviewed commit instead.
#
# Format: one line per repo, <name>=<full 40-char commit sha>
# Valid names: any name in repos.manifest (agent-browser, anthropic-official, caveman,
# claude-mem, claude-skills, davila7, debug-skill, ida-pro-mcp, impeccable, rea,
# superpowers, taste-skill, vercel-design, wshobson)
# Note: wshobson and davila7 each appear as multiple lines in repos.manifest
# (one upstream clone, several curated subset paths) — a single pin line
# here covers all of a name's subset lines, since they share one clone.
# Unpinned repos keep tracking the latest default branch.
#
# To pin: look up the commit on GitHub, review the diff, then add e.g.
# caveman=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567

# Pinned 2026-11-04 to the commits installed and checked on Surya8991's machine.
# To update: python scripts/dependencies.py preview --profile full, review, then change the SHA.
agent-browser=6682da310c75bed8af340b39cc10b7f71bded155
anthropic-official=ca45fc496a3436251f191354091d557da31c15b5
caveman=2e068f735253cce28256744804785f01887d9646
